    - id: 6
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Manual Law Library
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "LAW LIBRARY \uFFFD 9.01\n\nThe Law Library provides assistance to
          prisoners in \nresearch and preparation of legal work. The Law \nLibrarian
          assists prisoners in requesting materials \uFFFD \nthey do not do the legal
          work for you.\n\nTo access the Law Library, sign up on the Law Library
          \nlist in your living area. Staff collect the list \nnightly. You must
          request access daily \uFFFD no one will \nbe automatically called.\n\nPrisoners
          may use the Law Library one hour per day.\n\nA prisoner has the right to
          receive assistance from \nanother prisoner in the use of the Law Library.
          A \nprisoner providing such assistance may not charge or \nreceive payment
          of any kind.\n\nLEGAL COPIES \uFFFD 9.02\n\nLegal copies cost 15 cents
          per page. Complete a \ndisbursement form with your name, offender number,
          \ndate, and number of copies. Copies will be returned \nwithin three working
          days.\n\nAn indigent prisoner may have copies made, as required \n\n\nYou'd
          have to sign up on a list today to get in \ntomorrow. You don't know where
          the list is yet.\nOne hour. That's what you get.\nYou file this away. You
          might need it.\n\n---"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 15
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 6
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 19
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 6
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 20
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 2264
        y: 302
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 7
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Manual Mail
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "GENERAL MAIL \uFFFD 3.01\n\nPrisoners are responsible for their own
          postage costs.\n\nYou may not receive postage stamps in the mail. \nStamps
          must be purchased through commissary.\n\nOutgoing mail must be addressed
          as follows:\n\n[Your name as booked]\nFairbanks Correctional Center\n1931
          Eagan Ave.\nFairbanks, AK 99701\n\nMail with any other return address will
          be sent back \nto you and will not be mailed out of the institution.\n\nThe
          institution will, at its expense, provide postage \nfor up to five pieces
          of mail per week for any \nprisoner determined to be indigent.\n\nDO NOT
          SEAL OUTGOING MAIL.\n\nYou'd need a stamp to send anything.\nStamps come
          from commissary.\nCommissary requires money.\nOr you qualify as indigent
          and submit a form.\nWhich requires a cop-out.\nWhich requires a form.\n\nYou
          close that loop in your head and leave it there.\n\n---"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 15
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 7
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 21
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 7
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 22
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
        m_PersistentCalls:
          m_Calls: []
      canvasRect:
        serializedVersion: 2
        x: 1848
        y: 302
        width: 160
        height: 30
    - id: 8
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Manual Phone
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "TELEPHONES \uFFFD 6.01\n\nTelephone service at this facility is operated
          by \nSecurus, Inc., a private contractor. It is not \naffiliated with any
          local or long distance providers \nin Alaska.\n\nThe telephones are in
          service between 8:00 a.m. \nand 10:00 p.m. daily.\n\nCalls are limited
          to 15 minutes.\n\nAll long distance calls must be collect. Phone cards
          \nand 800 numbers will not work. Prisoners cannot \nreceive incoming calls.\n\nThe
          person you are calling must open an account with \nSecurus in order to
          accept your call. They may do so \nby calling 1-800-844-6591. In some cases
          a deposit \nwill be required.\n\nAll prisoners are required to enter their
          pre-assigned \nPIN number when placing a call. Do not exchange or \nallow
          other prisoners to use your PIN.\n\nFor security reasons, the phones may
          be disabled at \nany time with little or no notice.\n\nFifteen minutes.\nThe
          person you want to call needs an account first.\nYou try to remember if
          they would know to set one up.\nYou don't know if they know you're here
          yet.\nYour PIN is on a slip of paper somewhere in your \nintake paperwork.
          You need to find that.\n\n---"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 15
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
      falseConditionAction: Block
      conditionPriority: 2
      outgoingLinks:
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 8
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 23
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      - originConversationID: 15
        originDialogueID: 8
        destinationConversationID: 15
        destinationDialogueID: 24
        isConnector: 0
        priority: 2
      conditionsString: 
      userScript: 
      onExecute:
