    - id: 10
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Manual RFI
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "REQUEST FOR INTERVIEW \uFFFD 10.01\n\nRequests for Interview (also
          called cop-outs) are used \nto communicate with all staff. If you have
          a question \nor need, it must be written on a Request for Interview \nform
          and submitted to the appropriate staff member \nor program area.\n\nIf
          you are unsure which program or staff member to \ncontact, address your
          request to the Shift Supervisor \nand it will be directed accordingly.\n\nCompleted
          forms are placed in the cop-out boxes located \non the walls of each living
          area. Shift Supervisors \npick up forms once every 24 hours.\n\nYour name
          and offender number must be on the form. \nState your reason briefly. Swearing
          and derogatory \nstatements are not permitted.\n\nRequests for Interview
          are required for the following:\n\uFFFD Law Library access\n\uFFFD Scheduled
          visitation\n\uFFFD Medical and dental services  \n\uFFFD Indigent supply
          orders\n\uFFFD Commissary special requests\n\uFFFD Classification questions\n\nThere
          is no other way to make a formal request to staff. \nIf it is not submitted
          in writing on the appropriate \nform, it will not be processed.\n\nYou
          look around the cell for the form. \nYou don't see one yet. \nEverything
          here requires a form you don't have yet \nto get the things you need to
          get the form.\n\n\n---"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
